OL,3,GNEWSAHalf of Cornwall's rubbish could
OL,4,Astill be recycled
OL,5,
OL,6,FHalf the rubbish from Cornwall's homes
OL,7,Fcould have been recycled or disposed of
OL,8,Fas food waste, a recent study has
OL,9,Fshown.
OL,11,FAccording to Cornwall Council,
OL,12,Frecycling has increased in the county
OL,13,Fby about 20% since weekly food waste
OL,14,Fand fortnightly recycling and rubbish
OL,15,Fcollections were introduced across the
OL,16,Fcounty in 2024.
OL,18,FBut recent analysis of rubbish from 500
OL,19,Fhomes across the county found many were
OL,20,Fstill putting items like food,
OL,21,Fbatteries, vapes, paper and glass in
OL,22,Fthe bin.
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,345,340,200,160,0,100
